# Survex Duplicate Detector {{VERSION}}

Package target: `{{TARGET}}`.

Find geometric duplicate candidates in a Survex spatial model. Both endpoints
must match within tolerance, allowing reversed direction. The default is **5%
of the shorter leg**. Results are saved as CSV for review; the input is preserved.

## Run the bundled demo

Keep this directory's executable, `docs/` and `examples/` together. Open a
terminal here. This native package requires no Go, Python or Survex installation
for the text demo. The [platform guide](docs/platforms.md) lists the six Linux,
macOS and Windows packages and their processor architectures.

On macOS or Linux with the matching native package:

```bash
./survex-duplicates examples/kataster/KATASTER.legs.dump --out duplicates.csv
./survex-duplicates examples/kataster/KATASTER.legs.dump --exclude-splays --out duplicates-without-splays.csv
```

On Windows, use PowerShell:

```powershell
.\survex-duplicates.exe examples/kataster/KATASTER.legs.dump --out duplicates.csv
.\survex-duplicates.exe examples/kataster/KATASTER.legs.dump --exclude-splays --out duplicates-without-splays.csv
```

The first report contains **218 pairs**, the second **60**. The complete
18,584-leg KATASTER snapshot, its text dump and all eight expected CSV reports
are included. See the [demo guide](examples/kataster/README.md) for report links,
hashes, provenance and reproduction commands.

## Review your model

```bash
./survex-duplicates "my cave.dump" --exclude-splays --out review.csv
./survex-duplicates "my cave.dump" --epsilon 0.05 --out review-5cm.csv
./survex-duplicates --version
./survex-duplicates --help
```

For Windows, use `.\survex-duplicates.exe` in place of `./survex-duplicates`.
Binary `.3d` input additionally requires Survex's `dump3d` on supported native
platforms. Saved text dumps need no Survex. A complete dump has a header and
final `STOP`; copied LEG lines alone are insufficient.

`--relative-percent 5` means **5%**; `--epsilon 0.05` means **5 cm**. Each limit
applies to both matched endpoints. Legs carrying `DUPLICATE` are excluded by
default. Add `--include-duplicates` for the full geometric audit. SPLAY legs
are included unless `--exclude-splays` is set.

Existing output files are protected. Choose a new filename, or add `--force`
to replace a report after successful processing. Open CSVs using UTF-8 and a
comma delimiter. A match identifies a candidate for review, not a measurement
that should automatically be deleted.

The [usage guide](docs/usage.md) explains every option, CSV columns, reversal,
station names and three real duplicate examples. The
[platform guide](docs/platforms.md) describes target compatibility
and filesystem behavior. Source builds, development checks and historical
evidence are in the [source repository](https://github.com/dlubom/survex-duplicates).

